          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "Depending on whether you mean **Newcastle upon Tyne (UK)** or **Newcastle, New South Wales (Australia)**, several consultancies specialize in business process automation and Microsoft Power Automate implementation:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Newcastle upon Tyne (UK)**\n\nNewcastle and the wider North East region have a strong cluster of Microsoft partners and workflow automation specialists:\n\n*   **JUST XRM**  \n    * **Profile:** A specialist consultancy based in Newcastle upon Tyne led by a Microsoft FastTrack Recognized Solution Architect (who also founded the North East D365 & Power Platform User Group).\n    * **Best for:** Enterprise-grade architecture, deep integrations between Power Automate and Dynamics 365/Dataverse, multi-stage approval systems, and robust governance/Application Lifecycle Management (ALM).\n*   **Waterstons** (Offices across the North East / Newcastle & Durham)  \n    * **Profile:** One of the most established technology and business consulting firms in the North East.\n    * **Best for:** High-level business process mapping, strategic hyper-automation, and scaling Power Automate into intelligent AI agent workflows (via Copilot Studio) with strict security and data governance.\n*   **Marra** (Newcastle Helix)  \n    * **Profile:** Based in the Newcastle Helix tech cluster, focusing specifically on rapid digital transformation and custom Power Platform development.\n    * **Best for:** Medium-sized businesses looking to digitize manual tasks, build end-to-end cloud flows, or implement Robotic Process Automation (RPA/Desktop flows).\n*   **SR1 Development**  \n    * **Profile:** Established in 2011 in Newcastle, specializing in SharePoint, Microsoft 365, and Power Platform development.\n    * **Best for:** Businesses whose day-to-day work lives inside Microsoft 365. They excel at digitizing departmental paper trails (PO approvals, leave management, onboarding, supplier tracking, and automated document generation).\n*   **Geordie Consulting**  \n    * **Profile:** A boutique Newcastle-based Power Platform partner.\n    * **Best for:** Projects where workflow automation goes hand-in-hand with analytics, automated reporting, and Power BI dashboards.\n*   **INO Cloud Consultants** (Collingwood Street)  \n    * **Profile:** Cloud and business solutions consultancy focusing on Microsoft cloud tools.\n    * **Best for:** Connecting Power Automate to Dynamics 365, multi-channel Teams/email notifications, and AI chatbots.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Newcastle, NSW (Australia)**\n\nIf your business is located in the Hunter/Newcastle region of Australia:\n\n*   **Inlight IT** (Maryville, Newcastle)  \n    * A local technology consultancy providing Power Platform design, environment configuration, governance policies, and automated workflows across Microsoft 365 and Dataverse.\n*   **First Focus** (Newcastle branch)  \n    * A national managed service provider and systems integrator with a local office, experienced in business process automation, RPA, and legacy system integration with Power Automate.\n*   **Office Experts Group** (Hunter & Newcastle services)  \n    * Specialists in custom Microsoft 365 solutions, workflow design, and replacing fragmented Excel/paper forms with Power Automate and Power Apps.\n\n---\n\n### **How to Choose the Right Partner**\n\nWhen shortlisting consultancies for a Power Automate project, consider asking:\n\n1. **Process Discovery vs. Pure Development:** Do they map and simplify the process *before* building, or do they simply automate an already inefficient manual process?\n2. **Environment Governance & ALM:** Will flows be created under named individual user accounts (a major risk if that person leaves) or deployed properly using service principals, solutions, and environment pipelines?\n3. **Cloud vs. Desktop (RPA):** If you need to interface with legacy on-premise systems without APIs, make sure they have specific experience with **Power Automate Desktop** and unattended RPA.\n4. **Handoff and Training:** Ensure the engagement includes run-books, error-handling documentation, and internal team upskilling so you can maintain common flows without paying ongoing retainer fees for basic changes.",
